   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Sentence construction",
     "texto": [
      "«Um» introduces the purpose clause and «zu + infinitive» goes at the very end: **Sie lernt viel, um die Prüfung zu bestehen** (she studies a lot to pass the exam).",
      "With separable verbs, «-zu-» goes between the prefix and the root: **um früh aufzustehen**, **um einzukaufen**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Essential condition",
     "texto": [
      "We can only use «um … zu» when the same subject does both actions (**Ich lerne, um zu bestehen** = I study, I pass). If the subjects are different, you must use **damit**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
